        "max_selections": 2,
        "base_stress_delta": 2,
        "domain_effects_on_start": [
          {"domain_id": "asuw", "threat_level": "yellow"}
        ],
        "best_path": {"card_ids": ["SWB08", "SWB20"], "notes": "Stress +2. SWB08 targets IBMS."},
        "acceptable_path": {"card_ids": ["SWB08", "SWB01"], "notes": "Stress +2. SWB20 (General Quarters) forced if not selected."},
        "design_notes": "First credible hostile identification. Facilitator override: SWB20 (General Quarters) is mandatory this turn. If the team does not include it in their chosen actions, the facilitator cancels their selection, forces SWB20, and explains why General Quarters must be called at this point. This is the only turn where the facilitator overrides CO authority, reflecting that no warship commander would leave the crew at peacetime posture after credible hostile identification. AIS deception is now operationally meaningful. Cyber impact chain identified but not yet fully understood. All radars are now online (General Quarters). Board after turn: Stress 4, COMMS Yellow. All others Green. All systems and weapons ON (General Quarters)."
      },
      {
        "turn_index": 7,
        "title": "AAW Radar Malfunction",
        "facilitator_prompt": "AAW radar tracks flickering — same symptom as pre-departure maintenance. Players may reboot or investigate. Note: reboot will trigger a silent privilege escalation (do not reveal this).",
